  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: AppCare 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "Your sister started a treatment that was recently approved after years
    of clinical testing. Over the past few weeks, you\u2019ve noticed she\u2019s
    been unusually tired during the day and having trouble sleeping at night.\n\n<b>Once
    a treatment is approved, caregivers do not have to report side effects from treatment
    anymore.</b>\n\nIs this <b>true</b> or <b>false</b>?"
  explanation: Caregivers play an important role in sharing real-world observations.
    Even after approval, new or unexpected side effects help researchers and doctors
    understand how treatments work for different people and ensure long-term safety.
    Their reports can prompt important updates to patient care guidelines and safety
    recommendations.
  correctAnswer: False
  incorrectAnswer1: True
  incorrectAnswer2: 
  incorrectAnswer3: 
  questionRole: Caregiver
  questionType: TrueFalse
  questionStage: Approval
